PASS C10.h.notN  [witness] G(I/2, J'/2) is not ipW-orthogonal: ipW(G e10, G e10) = 1/4 != 1 = ipW(e10, e10)
PASS C10.orth  [identity] N-CLASS gates are ipW-orthogonal: cnot preserves ipW (symbolic) and homMap(A)^T homMap(A) = homMap(A^T A) (symbolic A), so actC A, actT A preserve ipW for orthogonal A
PASS C10.t.posFwd  [witness] G(2I, 2J') fails posFwd at the same witness (value -1); its posInv is G(I/2, J'/2)'s posFwd; ipW(G e10, G e10) = 4 != 1
PASS C10.id0  [witness] id with z = 0: the frame holds trivially (both corners are 0), the unit clause fails; id with z = z3: the frame FAILS at prodState(-z3, z3)
PASS C10.idnotN  [identity] id is not N-CLASS: det(actC A (actT B phiW)) = -det A det B (symbolic; nonzero for orthogonal A, B), while id maps prodState x y to a table of rank 1 (symbolic x, y)
PASS C10.imp  [identity] improper control: controlled-(id, diag(1,1,-1)) with any coherence from its zero-set forms maps e1 (x) e3 to 0 (not injective)
PASS C10.imp.cc  [countercontrol] countercontrol: the proper family G(a, b) does NOT annihilate e1 (x) e3 for a = I, b = J'

